ge label next_arg_ $[ s ]\_ [ e_{n} ]$ , remove $e_{n}$ ;  
else  
    Connect $n_{p}$ to $n_{n}$ with edge label $[ s ]\_ [ e_{n} ]$ , remove $e_{n}$ ;  
end  
Procedure BridgePlaceholderAndElement $(p)$ Find the corresponding edge and node of $p$ as $e_{p}$ and $n_{p}$ ;  
if no correspondings found then return;  
if The nearest previous element $n_{e}$ exist then  
    Connect $n_{p}$ to $n_{e}$ with edge next_arg_ $[ e_{p} ]$ else  
    Find the nearest next element $n_{e}$ , connect $n_{p}$ to $n_{e}$ with edge prev_arg_ $[ e_{p} ]$ end  
Procedure ProcessSymbolNode $(n)$ Get the children set $C = \{c_{j}\}_{j=1}^{k}$ of $n$ and the corresponding edge set $\{e_{j}\}_{j=1}^{k}$ ;  
if $|C| = 1$ then  
    Connect parents of $n$ with the only child $c_{1}$ with label $[ n]$ ; Remove $n$ ; else  
    Compute $l = \max(L[c] \text{ for } c \text{ in } C) + 1$ ;  
    Connect $c_{j-1}$ to $c_{j}, j > 1$ with edge $[ n ]\_ l\_ [ e_{j} ]$ ; Remove $e_{j}, j > 1$ ;  
    Add suffix $[ n ]\_ l\_ [ e_{1} ]$ to all parent edge labels of $n$ ;  
    Replace $n$ with $c_{1}$ , preserving all edge connection;  
end
